   "check": "the fix",
   "finding": "The defect is as described. Restarts drawn as sums of a fixed 64-point bank allow only C(66, 3) = 45,760 phase-1 walks (about 1.46M points) and 2,080 starts per target. The fix (chained starts s <- s + B_k, tp <- tp + B_k from Q) keeps the log bookkeeping right: every target of all 1584 rerun rows verifies, and 36 dumped runs (258,048 targets) were verified independently. The diff f71b42cc4f..75dbc70b36 of examples/mt_fieldops.rs is exactly the five restart hunks, so ic4, ic5 and bsgs2 are untouched. All 528 v2 ic4/bsgs2 rows, made by the v2 binary (bbcc68cc), replay exactly from the fixed source. That justifies the merge.",
